{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082214Z_dev-05_staged_1a28", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not give a detection significance for the GCE, either in σ or as a test statistic. It only says that the fitted GCE flux is nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models. It adds that this \"alone does not establish its statistical significance.\" It also says the Δ(−2lnL) differences between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The GCE fit results are reported only as spectra, credible intervals and χ² values for DM-spectrum fits (e.g. χ²=27.50 for 12 dof for b b̄).", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.1"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "8"}]}, "turns": 8, "seconds": 15.573, "tool_calls": 9, "tool_result_chars": 61872, "input_tokens": 18, "output_tokens": 1206, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 21831, "cache_read_input_tokens": 91475, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:22:30+00:00"}
